  "contentPlaintext": "<bold>System Design Overview</bold>\nThis document provides a high-fidelity technical specification of our system components, relational storage models, data routing mechanics, and interface protocols. It translates our product requirements into a strict engineering design manual.\n<bold>1. Table of Contents</bold>\n1. Table of Contents\n2. Global Architecture Topology\n2.1 Microservices & Structural Decoupling\n2.2 Runtime Network Topology Map\n3. Persistence Tier & Data Storage Models\n3.1 Database Structural Relationships (ERD)\n3.2 Production Data Dictionary Sheets\n4. Service Interactions & Dynamic Processing Flows\n4.1 End-to-End Async Ingestion Flow\n5. Interface & Gateway Routing Protocols\n5.1 RESTful Endpoint Layout Matrix\n<bold>2. Global Architecture Topology</bold>\n<bold>2.1 Microservices & Structural Decoupling</bold>\nThe production ecosystem uses a decoupled, event-driven structural model. This ensures a clean separation of concerns between raw client data collection, business logic computations, and persistent datastores. Individual components operate as independent runtime environments, allowing layers to scale up during workload surges without exhausting host computing clusters.\n<bold>2.2 Runtime Network Topology Map</bold>\nThe platform topology isolates user-facing client frameworks from backend logic compute nodes and persistent database engines using a layered security model:\n┌─────────────────┐       ┌─────────────────┐       ┌─────────────────┐\n│ Client App Tier │ ───&gt;  │ API Edge Gateway│ ───&gt;  │ Core Logic Hub  │\n│ (React/TS SPA)  │       │ (Reverse Proxy) │       │ (Node/FastAPI)  │\n└─────────────────┘       └─────────────────┘       └───────┬─────────┘\n                                                            │\n                                                            ▼\n                                                    ┌─────────────────┐\n                                                    │ Relational Pools│\n                                                    │(PostgreSQL Data)│\n                                                    └─────────────────┘\n<bold>3. Persistence Tier & Data Storage Models</bold>\n<bold>3.1 Database Structural Relationships (ERD)</bold>\nThe entity schema relies on explicit relational structures to guarantee transaction tracking and data integrity across active processing cycles.\n┌───────────────────┐               ┌────────────────────┐\n│   TENANT_ACCOUNT  │               │ TRANSACTION_RECORD │\n├───────────────────┤               ├────────────────────┤\n│ PK account_uuid   │1 ─────────── 0*│ PK record_uuid     │\n│    corporate_email│               │ FK account_uuid    │\n│    password_hash  │               │    payload_cents   │\n└───────────────────┘               └────────────────────┘\n<bold>3.2 Production Data Dictionary Sheets</bold>\n<bold>3.2.1 Table Name: </bold><code>TENANT_ACCOUNT</code>\nField Identifier\nData Type Variant\nConstraint Profiles\nSystem Boundary Description\n<code>account_uuid</code>\n<code>UUID</code>\nPRIMARY KEY, NOT NULL\nGlobal unique account identification hash string.\n<code>corporate_email</code>\n<code>VARCHAR(255)</code>\nUNIQUE, INDEX, NOT NULL\nAuthenticated corporate corporate profile address.\n<code>password_hash</code>\n<code>VARCHAR(60)</code>\nNOT NULL\nSalted cryptographic key value representation.\n<bold>3.2.2 Table Name: </bold><code>TRANSACTION_RECORD</code>\nField Identifier\nData Type Variant\nConstraint Profiles\nSystem Boundary Description\n<code>record_uuid</code>\n<code>UUID</code>\nPRIMARY KEY, NOT NULL\nUnique sequential transaction tracing code string.\n<code>account_uuid</code>\n<code>UUID</code>\nFOREIGN KEY REFERENCES\nTracing reference back to creator identity record.\n<code>payload_cents</code>\n<code>BIGINT</code>\nNOT NULL, DEFAULT 0\nFinancial field tracked explicitly in lowest base.\n<bold>4. Service Interactions & Dynamic Processing Flows</bold>\n<bold>4.1 End-to-End Async Ingestion Flow</bold>\nThis sequence trace maps out the lifecycle of a high-volume batch data upload passing through the platform architecture:\nClient UI App                API Edge Gateway             Core Logic Hub           Relational Pools\n     │                              │                            │                        │\n     │ ── 1. Submit Batch File ────&gt;│                            │                        │\n     │                              │ ── 2. Route Payload Check ─&gt;│                        │\n     │                              │                            │ ── 3. Parse &amp; Write ──&gt;│\n     │ &lt;── 4. Return HTTP 202 ──────│                            │                        │\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Submit Batch File:</textStyle></bold> The Client UI App submits a raw file payload via a secure multi-part form call.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Route Payload Check:</textStyle></bold> The API Edge Gateway validates user session tokens and matches incoming headers against routing constraints.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Parse & Write:</textStyle></bold> The Core Logic Hub unpacks the file, checks inputs against the data dictionary, and writes records to the Relational Pools using bulk transactions.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Return HTTP 202:</textStyle></bold> The gateway drops the active user channel back to an idle state with a tracking code before the internal save tasks finish execution.\n<bold>5. Interface & Gateway Routing Protocols</bold>\n<bold>5.1 RESTful Endpoint Layout Matrix</bold>\n<bold>5.1.1 Submit Batch Transaction</bold>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Protocol Method:</textStyle></bold> <code>POST</code>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Network Access Path:</textStyle></bold> <code>/api/v1/transactions/ingest</code>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Request Payload Schema (JSON):</textStyle></bold>\n{\n  \"account_uuid\": \"f81d4fae-7dec-11d0-a765-00a0c91e6bf6\",\n  \"payload_cents\": 142500\n}\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Success Response Code:</textStyle></bold> <code>202 Accepted</code>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Success Output Payload (JSON):</textStyle></bold>\n{\n  \"status\": \"processing\",\n  \"tracking_hash\": \"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855\"\n}\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Error Failure Status Options:</textStyle></bold> <code>400 Bad Request</code> (Invalid JSON parameters), <code>401 Unauthorized</code> (Session token expired).",
